{"case_id":"T8013","gap_exists":false,"gap_type":[],"commit_induced":"NO","maintenance_needed":false,"confidence":96,"affected_functions":["xmlXIncludeRecurseDoc","xmlXIncludeLoadFallback","xmlXIncludeDoProcess"],"reason":"The commit adds and propagates the internal xmlXIncludeCtxt.incTotal counter and, under FUZZING_BUILD_MODE_UNSAFE_FOR_PRODUCTION, stops XInclude processing after 20 replacements. It does not add an entry point, protocol, configuration requirement, input semantic, or new attack surface. H0 already supplies parser options through xmlFuzzReadInt, structured main/entity data through xmlFuzzReadEntities and xmlFuzzMainEntity, and exercises xmlReadMemory, push parsing, and xmlReaderForMemory. Thus no material harness gap is shown, and the commit does not create a maintenance need.","evidence":["H0 derives opts from xmlFuzzReadInt and passes it to xmlReadMemory, xmlCtxtUseOptions, and xmlReaderForMemory, preserving input control over parser configuration.","H0 calls xmlFuzzReadEntities and xmlFuzzMainEntity and installs xmlFuzzEntityLoader, providing document and referenced-resource input state relevant to inclusion processing.","xmlXIncludeDoProcess only adds ctxt->incTotal++, a fuzz-build-only ctxt->incTotal >= 20 check, and otherwise retains the existing xmlXIncludeTestNode, xmlXIncludePreProcessNode, load, and replacement flow.","xmlXIncludeRecurseDoc and xmlXIncludeLoadFallback merely copy incTotal into nested contexts and copy the resulting value back; they introduce no new externally controlled state or API.","Compared with S0 + H0, S1 + H0 retains the same harness-reachable parser interfaces and inputs; the change is an internal fuzzing resource limit rather than an uncovered behavior surface."],"recommended_action":"No harness maintenance is needed for this commit."}
